 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Their saying «لا تنفروا في الحر» is framed («وقال بعضهم لبعض»). 83 keeps As-Sa'di's restriction (those who stayed without excuse and did not grieve). A house for «بمقعدهم» (leaving before «رسول الله») and «فاقعدوا», a sun for «في الحر» that leaves before «نار جهنم»; nothing drawn for the Fire. No motif on the Prophet ﷺ. 81, 83: short-word flags, listen. STAGING v4: c1 (81-82): a town by day (Al-Muyassar: they stayed in Medina; the expedition was in great heat). Two small groups of three men (those who stayed behind) sit in the town; a house plate on 81:3 (their staying, gone before the Messenger's name); the right group shakes its head on 81:7 (they disliked striving); the left group speaks to the right group on 81:15 (Al-Muyassar: some said to others); a sun plate on 81:19 (the heat) that leaves before 81:21. Nothing is drawn for the Fire, for their laughing or for their weeping (82); the camera holds on them. No gesture of joy. c2 (83) stays ambient: the Prophet's return to them, their asking his leave and his answer (an empty-side address, and fighting)."
 },
